jessica_pm: Quick heads up @here — we're starting the deprecation process for the legacy JS sync SDK (v1). Posting timeline, breaking changes, and action items below.

sam_docs: TL;DR — new docs site + step-by-step migration guide are live: https://docs.redwood.ai/js-migrate (includes codemods & sample app). :rocket:

jessica_pm: Timeline: 30 days — officially marked DEPRECATED in docs/npm. 90 days — soft sunset (no new features, security fixes only). 180 days — samples removed from our hosted examples and CI flagged for removal. Customers on Dedicated/Private get extended support windows (see chris_eng).

dom_engineer: Key breaking changes we flagged from runtime testing: `client.generate()` has been renamed to `client.createText()`. Streaming via `options.stream: true` has been replaced by the new `createStream()` helper. Also the client import path changes. Expect small shape changes in the response object (tokens -> segments).

chris_eng: For Dedicated/Private customers we will enable a compatibility toggle for up to 6 months after removal; account teams will reach out with specifics. If you manage enterprise customers, please compile a list of any pinned internal builds that reference the old package.

sam_docs: Migration checklist (short):
1) change import `import { RedClient } from '@redwood/sdk'` -> `import { RedClient } from '@redwood/sdk/client'`
2) rename calls `generate` -> `createText`
3) replace streaming code with `createStream()` util (example below)
4) run the codemod in the repo root: `npx @redwood/migrate-js --from=sync-v1`

sam_docs: ```js
// before
const res = await client.generate({ prompt: 'Summarize this' })
// after
const res = await client.createText({ input: 'Summarize this' })
// streaming (before)
for await (const chunk of client.generateStream(...)) { /* ... */ }
// streaming (after)
for await (const chunk of createStream(client, { input: '...' })) { /* ... */ }
```

olivia_support: Support plan: docs triage channel open, migration office hours scheduled next Tue 3pm PT, and a dedicated email alias for migration requests. We'll also pin a FAQ in #help and escalate blockers to eng on SLAs.

jessica_pm: Action items for SDK owners: add a top-level deprecation banner in the package README, publish a 1.0.0-deprecated tag, ensure CI runs the compatibility suite, and add the migration note to your changelog by end-of-day Friday. If you need extra hands, @sam_docs and @dom_engineer volunteered to help convert examples. :thumbsup:

